# Git flow

Never commit directly to `main`. All changes ship through PRs.

## Branch naming

`<type>/<short-kebab-slug>` where `<type>` matches the Conventional Commits type
of the eventual PR title.

Examples:
- `feat/session-picker-filter`
- `fix/mcp-connect-timeout`
- `refactor/remove-cwd-prop-drilling`
- `chore/bump-deps`

## PR titles — Conventional Commits (required)

PR titles MUST follow Conventional Commits: `<type>(<optional-scope>): <subject>`.

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `perf`, `docs`, `test`, `build`,
`ci`, `chore`, `style`, `revert`.

Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period, keep under ~72 chars.

Examples:
- `feat(cli): add --continue flag`
- `fix(session): avoid crash on corrupt session JSON`
- `refactor: remove cwd prop drilling, centralize in config/paths`
- `chore(deps): bump vitest to 2.1`

The PR title becomes the squash commit title on `main` (`squash_merge_commit_title: PR_TITLE`), so treat it as the permanent changelog entry.

## PR body

The PR body becomes the squash commit message (`squash_merge_commit_message: PR_BODY`). Keep it useful for future readers:

```
## Summary
- bullet points describing the change

## Test plan
- [x] what was verified
- [ ] what still needs manual verification
```

## Merge strategy

Squash merge only. `main` stays linear.
- `allow_squash_merge: true`, `allow_merge_commit: false`, `allow_rebase_merge: false`
- Branches are auto-deleted on merge (`delete_branch_on_merge: true`).

## Enforcement

These conventions are enforced automatically:

- **Commit messages**: `commitlint` with `@commitlint/config-conventional` runs via a Husky `commit-msg` hook (`.husky/commit-msg`). Configured in `commitlint.config.js`. Installed on `npm install` via the `prepare` script.
- **PR titles**: GitHub Action `.github/workflows/pr-title.yml` (using `amannn/action-semantic-pull-request`) fails the check on any PR whose title is not Conventional Commits. Make it a required status check on `main` in branch protection so such PRs cannot be merged.

If the hook or action is ever misbehaving, fix the config — do not bypass with `--no-verify` or by disabling the workflow.

## Commit hygiene

- Never mention Cursor, the agent, the assistant, or AI tooling in commit messages, PR titles, or PR bodies.
- Never `--no-verify` or skip hooks.
- Never force-push to `main`. Avoid `--amend` on commits that were already pushed.
- Only commit when the user explicitly asks.
